{
  "schema": 1,
  "spec": "The RetroDECK component launchers ES-DE can run, each pinned by the git blob hash of its deployed copy, and the variables it reads that RetroDECK's own start provides, in the order it first reads them. A variable is defined in one start file (variables), pinned by its own blob hash (start_files); a launcher's pin covers the start file of every variable it reads. Values are read live, never packaged: a 'line' variable from its assignment in the start file, a 'paths' variable from retrodeck.json's paths, which conf_read exports under the key's own name at line. Read by atlas.launch_environment; held against the deployed Flatpak by tests/test_launch_environment_tripwire.py.",
  "retrodeck": {
    "version": "0.10.10b",
    "start": "bin/retrodeck:40 sources /app/libexec/global.sh; global.sh:16-18 sources logger.sh and :116-118 all_vars.sh under allexport; conf_read (other_functions.sh:148-190, called at global.sh:198 and :210) exports every key of retrodeck.json's paths and options; global.sh:231-233 sources every component's component_functions.sh under allexport (source_component_functions, other_functions.sh:1370-1424); start_esde (retrodeck/components/es-de/component_functions.sh:9-12) runs ES-DE's launcher in a child bash, and ES-DE hands each command to /bin/sh, so every export reaches a component launcher"
  },
